T = [
("THE ASTRALITE MATRIX","matrix",[
 "Field note 1. Every living thing out here carries a signature. Beasts, people, the grass under my boots. Twenty years looking for an exception. Stopped looking.",
 "Zarvane, second season. Their readers see the signature before they see the animal. I asked one to teach me. He said you cannot teach a man to have been born here.",
 "Andrannor. Watched a splicer force one signature to hold two shapes. It worked. Something paid for the second shape and it was not the splicer.",
 "Veridan. The root-scribes count NINE FAMILIES in the lattice. Would not tell me how they counted. Only that the ninth one counts you back.",
 "Netharion archive, week six. Nine families, seven tiers. Sixty-three Astralites. There is a sixty-fourth line on the page and no ink has ever stayed on it.",
 "Vorashil. Told the embassy my sixty-fourth theory. They were kind about it. The sixty-fourth is not a fourth anything — it is what the other sixty-three are measured AGAINST.",
 "Xilnar. The dead still carry signature. Whatever the Matrix is, it is not a property of being alive. It is a property of having BEEN. I sat with that for a week.",
 "Baelgor. Went home. Read the Pledge again with Matrix notation in my head. The founders were not being poetic, son. They were filing a claim.",
 "Thardin. Their instruments WRITE to the lattice now. The Ministry calls it manufacturing. Every older word I know for it means forgery.",
 "Korathen. Last entry on this. The Matrix is not a map of what exists. It is the list of what is ALLOWED to exist. Somebody wrote that list and I would like a word."]),

("THE TWENTY-SEVEN WORLDS","worlds",[
 "The Malezor schoolyard has a counting rhyme that ends at twenty-seven. Asked four teachers what it counts. Four shrugs.",
 "Zarvane. The oasis readers say the sky holds twenty-seven true stars and the rest is weather. I laughed. They did not.",
 "Andrannor slang for a hopeless errand: 'ask the twenty-seventh.' Nobody can tell me why it is funny. It stopped being funny to me.",
 "Veridan Seedvault. Three specimens grew under a different sun. The labels give a NUMBER, not a name. Ours is nine.",
 "Netharion. There it is in the Null Observatory, plain as a ledger. Twenty-seven worlds, ordered — and not by distance. We are Ax-9.",
 "Vorashil. Every visitor arrives already knowing our number. All of them are mildly disappointed by it. I have stopped asking why.",
 "Xilnar. The Blackwake Chapel keeps twenty-seven wicks lit for the dead of worlds that are not this one. Six had gone out when I counted. Nobody relights them.",
 "Baelgor University. They teach the Expanse as HISTORY, not astronomy. The worlds were not discovered, son. They were assigned.",
 "Thardin. The Anomaly Engine can hear the other twenty-six. The Ministry logs it as industrial noise and files it unopened. I have the file numbers.",
 "Korathen. Twenty-seven is not a count of places. It is a count of ATTEMPTS. Nine are still running. I do not know what happened to the other eighteen and I am afraid I do."]),

("AETHRYX","aethryx",[
 "Kelthor said the word once, in twenty years. Would not say it twice. Told me it is not a word for a beastwarden's mouth. He has never refused me anything else.",
 "Zarvane. Their elders bow before speaking it. Asked three of them why. None could tell me. The reflex is older than the reason.",
 "Andrannor. They use it as a curse in the clubs. The oldest patrons still flinch. Habits outlive belief out here.",
 "Veridan. Parliament records the name in a script used for nothing else and taught to no one. I copied nine characters. I have never found the tenth.",
 "Netharion. The Impossible Archive is blunt about it: AETHRYX is not one of the sixty-three. It is the REASON there are sixty-three.",
 "Vorashil, Unmouth Academy. AETHRYX is not a being with a signature. It is the condition under which a signature is possible at all. Took me a month to write that sentence down.",
 "Xilnar. The dead do not fear it. I have thought about that more than anything else in this notebook and I still do not like where it goes.",
 "Baelgor. The Pledge was sworn TO something and the founders never wrote what. The blank space is exactly nine letters wide. I measured it twice.",
 "Thardin. They tried to instrument it. Every device returned the reading it was calibrated to expect. Every time. That is not how instruments work, son. That is how a mirror works.",
 "Korathen. The Gemlords do not claim to serve AETHRYX. They claim to have been NOTICED by it. Once. Each. That is the whole of their authority."]),

("THE GEMLORDS","gemlords",[
 "Rakoron sleeps under our feet and the ground above him is warm in winter. Kelthor says that is not a metaphor. I have taken the temperature. It is not.",
 "Zarvane. Ivirium's pearl-light is why their night is never fully dark. The oasis remembers being watched. Their word for dusk means 'the looking'.",
 "Andrannor. Mutaryn changed shape so often the citrine kept the last one out of politeness. That is what a local told me. I believe him.",
 "Veridan. Emeralix does not rule here. Veridan GREW around the place Emeralix stopped walking. The parliament is a scar tissue.",
 "Netharion. Eurakeon's amethyst is the only Fathergem that answers a question with a question. Asked it about your mother. Still thinking about the reply.",
 "Vorashil. Azurel wept once and the tear did not fall — it crystallised in the air. Everything this district knows about clarity comes out of that one moment.",
 "Xilnar. Obsidius is not a keeper of the dead. He is the reason death is a DOOR here and not a wall. The distinction matters enormously to the people who live here.",
 "Baelgor. Ambrevon's amber holds the first settlement whole. Bread still on the table. He has never explained why he kept it and no one has ever dared ask twice.",
 "Thardin. Oathane consented to the Accord last and regretted it first. I got twenty minutes with him. He spent nineteen of them silent.",
 "Korathen. The Council seats TEN. I have watched it convene four times. It has never once seated ten. Look at the empty chair and count the dust on it."]),

("WHAT A ZYREX IS","zyrex",[
 "First rule, and I have never had to revise it: a Zyrex is not an animal that happens to glow. It is a signature that happens to have a body.",
 "Zarvane. Their children see the signature before the creature and find it unremarkable. Their adults find it exhausting. I understand both.",
 "Andrannor proved a Zyrex CAN hold two signatures. It did not prove one should. I have seen the ones that came out of that and I did not sleep well.",
 "Veridan. Every Zyrex is bound to terrain. Take one far enough from where its signature was written and it does not die — it FORGETS. That is worse.",
 "Netharion. Tier is not strength. Tier is the WIDTH of signature a body can carry without tearing. Everything the academies teach about power is a mistranslation of that.",
 "Vorashil, Manybody Habitat. They keep one with no fixed body at all. Filed as a single specimen. It disagrees, and it has said so.",
 "Xilnar. Signature persists after the body stops. That is why this district is loud at night and why nobody here thinks that is strange.",
 "Baelgor. Humanoids are Humanoid-PRIMARY. Zyrex never are. One line, and it is why we are different in KIND and not in degree. Your mother explained it to me before any professor did.",
 "Thardin has built a body and put a signature inside it. The Ministry calls the result a Zyrex. Nothing else does — not the Zyrex, not the ground, not me.",
 "Korathen. A Zyrex is a sentence the Matrix is still in the middle of writing. Bonding one is asking to read over its shoulder. Be polite about it."]),

("THE VERDANT AWAKENING","verdant",[
 "Our oldest farmers date everything from 'the green year'. Not one of them can tell me WHICH year. Every almanac in Malezor is missing the same page.",
 "Zarvane. There is a layer of pollen in the sand from a world that has no flowers. I have a sample. Three labs have declined to test it.",
 "Andrannor. Every hybrid traces back to one event. The Exchange calls it the First Splice and is careful never to call it an accident.",
 "Veridan IS the Awakening. They do not commemorate it — the parliament is what it BECAME. Standing in that chamber is standing inside the event.",
 "Netharion. It was not growth. It was a signature spilling out of its container and finding a million new ones in an afternoon.",
 "Vorashil. Their visitors call it an INFECTION and are then asked politely to leave. I have watched that exchange four times and the wording never varies.",
 "Xilnar. The dead from before the Awakening carry no signature at all. None. Whatever happened, it happened TO everything, at once, and it happened here.",
 "Baelgor University, unpopular thesis, mine: every Viridian creature is a BY-PRODUCT. The Awakening was aimed at something else and missed. They did not renew my lecture.",
 "Thardin. Their cores show the Awakening had a source point and it was not on this world. I have the readout. I have not shown it to anyone.",
 "Korathen. It was a REPLY. Something asked, and the green answered on behalf of a planet that had not agreed to speak for itself."]),

("THE SIXTEEN PRISMS","prisms",[
 "A prism in the Malezor market is a pretty stone and goes for pretty-stone money. Kelthor will pay forty times that and will not tell me why.",
 "Zarvane. The oasis has swallowed three prisms in living memory and returned none of them. They still throw them in.",
 "Andrannor fences prism fragments openly. The real ones never reach the market twice. I have watched a stall lose one and go quiet for a year.",
 "Veridan Seedvault holds a prism that GROWS. That is not what prisms do. The vault keeper agrees and keeps feeding it.",
 "Netharion counts SIXTEEN. All sixteen named, fifteen placed. The archive is entirely confident about the sixteenth and will not write it down for me.",
 "Vorashil. A prism does not store power. It stores a PERMISSION — and the holder is the one being permitted. Read that twice, son. I had to.",
 "Xilnar. The Last Lantern runs on a prism nobody has replaced in nine hundred years. They do not consider this remarkable. I do.",
 "Baelgor. The Pledge names the prisms as WITNESSES to the founding, not tools of it. Witnesses can be called back to testify.",
 "Thardin mass-produces three — Zysphere, Zycube, Zyramid — and calls them utility prisms. The other thirteen are not for sale and, I am told, not for making.",
 "Korathen. The sixteenth is the KEY OF ANCIUXOR. It does not open a thing. It opens a PERMISSION. And the permission is the ending."]),

("THE BONDING VESSELS","vessels",[
 "Page four of my first notebook, kept it all these years: the Zysphere is new. What it DOES is not. I was twenty-three and already sure.",
 "Zarvane's dunes give up shards of something older than glass. The readers call them Prismshards and handle them like relics. They are right to.",
 "Andrannor sells replica Prismshards to tourists. Two of the replicas have bonded something. The stall owner has stopped selling them and will not say more.",
 "Veridan. An old root grew around a Prismshard and will not release it. The tree is measurably healthier for it. I have twelve years of measurements.",
 "Netharion. Confirmed in writing at last: the Prismshard is the direct progenitor of the Zysphere. Every sphere Thardun sells is a copy of a thing FOUND, not invented.",
 "Vorashil. The Prismshard did not capture. It OFFERED. That difference is the whole of Kelthor's eighth step and I did not understand it until I stood here.",
 "Xilnar. They bury their dead holding shards. The dead were buried holding the thing that held them. I had to step outside after that one.",
 "Baelgor. The first Pledge was sworn on a Prismshard, not a book. Someone swapped them later. No record of who, and the swap is not in the minutes.",
 "Thardin's mass-market sphere opens at five percent bond. The Prismshard would not open below ninety-five. Convenience cost something and we are still paying it.",
 "Korathen. A Prismshard is a Gemlord's fingerprint left in stone. Every one you ever hold, one of THEM touched first. Hold them accordingly."]),

("CYTHERION","cytherion",[
 "The beetles in our fields are wrong. Wrote that in year one with 'wrong HOW?' beside it. Twenty years later the second half is still blank.",
 "Zarvane. Sand-mantises hunt in formation. Nothing taught them the formation. I checked. I checked for two seasons.",
 "Andrannor Menagerie keeps a spider that builds to a PLAN. I sketched the plan. The plan is not the spider's.",
 "Veridan. Insects predate every other lineage on this world by an order that should be impossible. The root-scribes shrug. It is not their problem.",
 "Netharion gave me the name at last: CYTHERION. The eighth world. Nine point two billion years ago. It is not there any more.",
 "Vorashil. The Cytherion war was Spider against Mantis and it was not about territory. It was about whose PLAN the Grid would run. That is a war I understand.",
 "Xilnar. The oldest dead here are not human and not Zyrex. The chapel calls them the First Mourners and will not be drawn further.",
 "Baelgor. The Grid SURVIVED Cytherion. It has been looking for a substrate ever since. We are a substrate. I wrote that and then sat down.",
 "Thardin. The Anomaly Engine runs on principles nobody at the Ministry designed. Go and compare its lattice to a mantis nest. Go on.",
 "Korathen. Mykarlyth came out of Cytherion, and Mykarlyth is why the Expanse has rules at all. The Bug War wrote our physics as a PEACE TREATY."]),
]

T2 = [
("THE SEERS","seers",[
 "The hooded ones in our east fields are not from Malezor. Kelthor has stopped pretending otherwise and so have I.",
 "Zarvane. Their Seer post takes more than it gives. The Elder keeps the ledger, knows the difference exactly, and says nothing. I would say something.",
 "Andrannor. The clubs are full of Seer money. Owners who ask where it came from stop being owners. I asked once, from a safe distance.",
 "Veridan. The Hospice treats Seer-burn. No heat in the wound and it does not close. Your mother would know what to do with it. I did not.",
 "Netharion. Ophira runs the visible campaign and is not the POINT of it. Watch the ritual UNDER the campaign. I watched for eleven nights.",
 "Vorashil. Orryx and Ophira answer to XENOXIL, the Flesh Lord. And Xenoxil is not destabilising the districts — it is CONNECTING them. That is far worse.",
 "Xilnar. What they siphon is not power. It is CONSENT. Ask a world enough times and it stops noticing it was asked. I have started counting how often I say yes.",
 "Baelgor. They will take people to make a point about leverage, and the point will not be aimed at the people. Remember that if it is ever aimed at us.",
 "Thardin. Every tower they darkened was a mouth. Ten mouths, one throat. Scrapjaw worked that out before any of us and nobody listened to him either.",
 "Korathen. They are not conquering Zyraxis. They are PREPARING it — and the preparation only works if the ten districts become one system. Do not help them make it one."]),

("THE NOVARIAN CHALLENGE","novarian",[
 "Our Coliseum runs a bracket every season and not one person in the stands can tell me who Novarius was. I asked forty.",
 "Zarvane. Their Invitational is older than their town hall. The hall has a founding stone. The bracket does not need one.",
 "Andrannor. The bracket has been fixed twice and voided both times by something nobody has been able to identify. I checked the paperwork. There is none.",
 "Veridan will not host on parliament ground. No reason given. None accepted either — I pushed, and was walked to the door politely.",
 "Netharion records: NOVARIUS was the first Beast Master. Not the first Rizer. The first to be ANSWERED. Sat down when I read that.",
 "Vorashil. The Challenge is not a tournament. It is the surviving form of an EXAMINATION. Something used to sit that exam and something used to mark it.",
 "Xilnar holds every Novarian champion. All of them, every district, always. Somebody is collecting them and it is not chance.",
 "Baelgor. The Accord sanctioning the Challenge was signed by OATHANE. A Gemlord underwrote a sporting event. I have never got a straight answer as to why.",
 "Thardin. The Seers have moved nine times to have the Challenge abolished and once to have it destroyed outright. That tells you what it is worth.",
 "Korathen. It measures whether a bonded pair can be TRUSTED with what comes next. The Seers want it gone because they intend to fail it. Win it, son."]),

("THE RIZER PATH","rizer",[
 "Kelthor's first step is not a technique. It is standing still long enough to be assessed. Most people cannot do it and I was most people.",
 "Zarvane. Omniris teaches THE SIGHT where Kelthor teaches THE BOND, and each insists the other is the prerequisite. They are both right, which is inconvenient.",
 "Andrannor's academies sell shortcuts. Their graduates never bond above tier two and cannot say why. I can say why. Nobody pays me to.",
 "Veridan. Bond capacity is not affection. It is how much of another signature you can hold without losing the shape of your OWN. I have seen men lose the shape.",
 "Netharion. The ladder is tier times three hundred and thirty-three. Not arbitrary — it is the width of the lattice, divided. Everything fits once you see it.",
 "Vorashil. A Rizer at full bond holds three thousand three hundred and thirty. A Gemlord requires ALL of it. That is not a difficulty setting, that is a door.",
 "Xilnar. Bond survives the body. Their dead are still bonded to things, and the things still come when called. I have watched it happen.",
 "Baelgor. Humanoid and Zyrex run the SAME progression. Zyrex evolve, humanoids rize. One system, two verbs. Took me eleven years to be sure of that sentence.",
 "Thardin sells bond-acceleration and it works. What it accelerates is not the bond. I could not get anyone to explain what it does accelerate.",
 "Korathen. The path does not end in power. It ends in being ASKED something — and having enough of yourself left to answer. Keep enough of yourself."]),

("THE TWENTY TYPES","types",[
 "My type chart has twenty columns. I have redrawn it four times and thrown away three. The fourth is in the lab if you want it.",
 "Zarvane. Their readers see type before creature — they describe it as reading the handwriting before the letter. Best description I have found.",
 "Andrannor. Hybrids hold two types and pay for the second in lifespan. The Exchange does not put that on the paperwork. I would.",
 "Veridan. Type is not element. Type is which of the nine FAMILIES a signature was drawn from. Every schoolbook on Zyraxis has this wrong.",
 "Netharion. Nineteen types answer to each other in a closed ring. The twentieth answers to nothing, and everything answers to it.",
 "Vorashil. ULTIMATE is not a strong type. It is an UNANSWERED one. Triple against all, no weakness — because there is nothing above it to object.",
 "Xilnar. SPIRIT is the only type the dead keep. Everything else turns out to be a property of having a body. That reframed my whole chart.",
 "Baelgor. Creature, then Beast, then Draconic. Not a power ladder — a ladder of how much the world lets you DECIDE. Your mother said it first, over dinner.",
 "Thardin manufactures TECH. It is the only type with a founding date, and therefore the only one that can be revoked. Somebody should be worried about that.",
 "Korathen. The twenty are the nine families times the tiers, FOLDED. Somebody folded them. The fold is the interesting part and nobody will discuss it."]),

("THE VOID SEAS","void",[
 "Our coast has a hard edge and nothing swims past it. We tell the children the sea is deep. It is not deep. I have measured.",
 "Zarvane. Caravans will not camp within sight of the border and change the subject well when asked. Best-drilled evasion I have met.",
 "Andrannor. Smugglers have tried the Void by boat eleven times. Eleven boats came back. No crews. The boats were undamaged.",
 "Veridan. Their rivers run to the border and STOP. Not drain, not sink — stop. I stood in one for an hour trying to see the mechanism.",
 "Netharion. The Void Seas are not water and not distance. They are the MARGIN OF THE PAGE. Once you read that you cannot unread it.",
 "Vorashil. Their visitors crossed something to get here and none of them crossed the Void. There is another way in and they will not name it.",
 "Xilnar. The dead do not go into the Void. Whatever it is, it is not where things GO. That ruled out my three best theories in one afternoon.",
 "Baelgor. The Old Conquest ended at the Void. The New Conquest was the admission that it always would. We keep having to learn the same edge.",
 "Thardin has mapped the Void's edge to the tile and the map is UNIFORM. Nothing natural is uniform, son. Nothing.",
 "Korathen. The Void is the boundary of the ATTEMPT. Twenty-seven worlds, each with a margin. The Bridge of Hope crosses one of them. Only one."]),

("THARDUN","thardun",[
 "Every Zysphere in Malezor carries a maker's mark and not one person in this town has met the maker. I have written to them nine times.",
 "Zarvane stocks Thardun goods that Thardun has no record of shipping. Showed the manifest to a rep. He asked to keep it.",
 "Andrannor launders Thardun surplus. The surplus is larger than the production. I ran the numbers twice because I assumed I was wrong.",
 "Veridan bans Thardun instruments on parliament ground and the ban is OLDER than the instruments. Somebody knew what was coming.",
 "Netharion. Thardun the CORPORATION is not Thardin the district. The names were close enough to be useful to somebody, and still are.",
 "Vorashil. Thardun did not invent the Zysphere. It found one, copied it badly, and sold the copy at a price the original never had.",
 "Xilnar. The Orphan Foundry is named honestly. That is the single most alarming thing I have learned in this district.",
 "Baelgor. The Precision Ministry exists to certify Thardun's work is safe. The Ministry is a Thardun DEPARTMENT. It is on their org chart, page nine.",
 "Thardin. The Anomaly Engine was not built. It was EXCAVATED. They have been reverse-engineering their own foundation for a century and calling it R&D.",
 "Korathen. Thardun's real product is not spheres. It is the idea that a bond can be BOUGHT. That idea is doing exactly what it was released to do."]),

("THE EMPTY THRONE","throne",[
 "Our hall has ten seats carved into the beam and one is left unpainted. 'Tradition,' they say. Nobody can tell me the tradition.",
 "Zarvane sets ten cups at solstice and pours nine. Watched an old woman do it alone, in the dark, when she thought nobody was looking.",
 "Andrannor's Tenfold Forum has a tenth podium never once used and dusted daily. The cleaner has done it forty years. I asked. She just shrugged.",
 "Veridan's parliament leaves a gap in the root-ring. Nobody cut that gap. The trees grew around it on their own.",
 "Netharion, plainly: OATHEUS, Tenth Gemlord of Korathen, is ABSENT. Not dead. The archive is very specific about that distinction and repeats it twice.",
 "Vorashil. An absent Gemlord means an unclaimed Fathergem, and an unclaimed Fathergem means an open seat in a council that governs by CONSENT. Do the arithmetic.",
 "Xilnar. Obsidius would know if Oatheus had died. Obsidius says nothing. The district reads that silence as an answer and I think they are right.",
 "Baelgor. The Pledge requires ten signatories and has nine. Every law built on it is provisional. Everyone has agreed not to mention this.",
 "Thardin. Oathane consented LAST and regretted it FIRST. He may be the only one alive who knows where the tenth went. He gave me nineteen silent minutes.",
 "Korathen. The Empty Throne is not a vacancy. It is a QUESTION left open on purpose — and answering it is what ends this. I do not know who it was left open for."]),

("THE MIGRATION","migration",[
 "Our oldest families cannot trace back past a certain generation. The records do not thin out, son. They BEGIN.",
 "Zarvane's language has words for landscapes Zarvane does not have. Six of them. I have the list. Three describe ice.",
 "Andrannor is a port town with no port and has been since founding. Their oldest guild is still the Harbourmasters.",
 "Veridan grows three crops with no wild ancestor anywhere on this world. They are the three that feed the most people.",
 "Netharion. The wave was MIXED. Not one people fleeing — several, together. That is rarer and far harder, and it means somebody organised it.",
 "Vorashil is called the Alienlands because it is where they LANDED, not where they came from. Everyone gets that backwards, including me for nine years.",
 "Xilnar buries by origin-world and has run out of categories twice. The second time they stopped adding and started a second cemetery.",
 "Baelgor. The Hall of First Settlement dates the arrival. Two hundred million years in transit — and the hall does not explain how anything survived it.",
 "Thardin. The ships are still out there. The Anomaly Engine hears them and the Ministry files it as noise. I have the file numbers for that too.",
 "Korathen. They did not flee Cytherion. They were SENT. And the sending is still in progress. We are the middle of somebody's plan, not the end of one."]),

("DREAMLAND","dream",[
 "Sleep in Malezor and you dream of somewhere with no ground. Everyone does. Nobody compares notes. I started comparing notes.",
 "Zarvane's readers dream in the Blue and wake able to see one thing they could not see before. One thing. Never two.",
 "Andrannor sells dream-suppressants and sales are strongest among people who have been to Vorashil. That correlation is not subtle.",
 "Veridan's Hospice treats people who did not come back from a nap. They are breathing. They are simply still there.",
 "Netharion. Dreamland is not imagination. It is a PLANE — the Blue Gem's plane. The Blue Gem is the one nobody wanted and now I know why they should have.",
 "Vorashil. A Rizer in Dreamland meets THEMSELVES. That is not a warning, it is the mechanism. I met mine. We did not get on.",
 "Xilnar. The dead are IN Dreamland. That is why this district sleeps in shifts and never alone. I took the second shift and did not sleep at all.",
 "Baelgor. The Ultimate Amplified Form needs pure balance of Blue and Purple — brain and soul, held level. Dreamland is where that gets TESTED, not learned.",
 "Thardin cannot instrument Dreamland and has quietly stopped publishing the attempts. Nine papers, then nothing, then a new department.",
 "Korathen. Everyone who has ever bonded is in Dreamland right now, asleep or not. The Gemlords have been holding that door shut with their bodies. All ten of them. Nine."]),
]
T = T + T2
